===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ar|شَرِيعَة|lit=path, way}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|Islam}} [[traditional|Traditional]] [[Islamic]] [[religious]] [[law]] primarily based on the [[Quran]], but also the [[hadith]] and [[tafsir]]; it covers the [[totality]] of religious, [[political]], [[social]] and [[private]] [[life]], making no [[distinction]] between religion and life – in other words between transgressions of moral rules ([[sin]]) and of social rules.
#: ''The legislation of '''shari'a''' law here is very strict.''

